Well, it's definitely harder to get help online when you have a large and/or proprietary app. Here's a great article <https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/help.html> with general tips, including how to make a minimal reproducible example (MRE). In you case, this means having a minimal module and minimal app code, just enough to show the problem. Crucially, it has to be copy-pasteable and runnable. The longer I have to spend getting your code to even run, the less time I'll have to actually help. It also helps a lot to have data that is copy-pasteable (in this case, an in-memory data frame or tibble), rather than making me download a file. That takes care of the large part. The proprietary part requires you to create dummy data with the same structure.

I'll try to take a look at this later today, but if you can get a better MRE, that will go a long way.

